Card 2:
  Fields: ['6ec95ca3-29e8-4b1b-bd53-36515cf00617', "Grammar words might fry your brain:What's the second person plural of the perfect tense for 'dar'?Huh?Instead, the deck drops youright in the middle of the sentenceand gives you visual cues:↧ En aquel momento, de repente, ↧vosotros […dar…]{{c1::Some visual cues:⊙ This happens right now. ⊙← This used to happen. ←↧ This happened in that exact moment. ↧→ This will happen. →See the manual for all the verbal and visual cues.::…OK…}}", '', '']
  Tags:  orientation 

Card 3:
  Fields: ['15d669b8-cf3d-4edd-905a-2101f980742a', "For beginners, the idea behind the deck is thatyou learn all Spanish conjugation in one go.Even before you start properly studying Spanish, if you like!This is an amazing language-learning hack.The manual explains why.{{c1::If you follow my method,instead of adding a few cards a dayyou'll add a whole verb at a time.To know how many cards to addfor the next verb,you can consult the deck descriptionin the manualand even paste it in the Description field under the deck's Options.01. Ser (to be): 58 cards02. Haber (to have): 59 cards03. Estar (to be): 57 cards04. Hablar (to speak): 59 cards05. Deber (to have to): 59 cards(…)::…OK…}}", '', '']
  Tags:  orientation 

Card 4:
  Fields: ['7766a47e-0272-459e-a8a9-5e11c006b8e0', "For advanced learners, you can filter the deck(using extremely specific tags)in order to drill down on a specific part of Spanish conjugation.{{c1::You'll find the full list of tags inthe Filtering section of the manual andI recommend you paste this version inthe Description field under the deck's Options.For instance:1. By Subjecttag:yotag:tú_vos…2. By Tensetag:presentetag:imperfecto…3. By Verb Endingtag:ends_in_ar…4. By Spanish Verb Nametag:sonreír…5. By Level of Regularitytag:regular_verbtag:irregular_verbtag:regular_formtag:high_irregularity…6. Misc Tagstag:regular_spelling_changetag:idiom…::…OK…}}", '', '']
  Tags:  orientation 

Card 5:
  Fields: ['fa7b5373-e4e6-4256-b7c2-d2826c17e35a', "During normal usage you'll justswipe left or right (if on mobile.)But when you are confused about a verb form or curious to learn morethe card shows lots of extra details.{{c1::For instance,1. Conjugations for Verbs in the same Familydesoigo←desoírentreoigo←entreoír(the links takes you to the DLE.)2. Spelling ExplanationsThe spelling change oió → oyó is considered regular (preserves spelling rules and pronunciation)3. How exactly a Form is irregularIrregular form: the hypothetical regular form habieron is incorrect. 4. Stats about the VerbRegular formoír : moderate irregularity, #37 in the deck out of 60 dissonant verbs, 13 counts (23%)5. Sometimes even Idioms!refrán: no hay mal que por bien no venga (~ every cloud has a silver lining)For more, read Anatomy of a Flashcard.::…OK…}}", '', '']
  Tags:  orientation 

